        <div id="why-epoxy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Garage Floor Epoxy Buying Guide: Is Epoxy Worth It?
          </h2>
          <p>
            Bare concrete is one of the most hostile surfaces in a home. It's porous, which means oil, antifreeze, and brake fluid soak in permanently and become eyesores. It dusts continuously — that gray powder on your car tires and tools comes from the concrete surface abrading under foot and vehicle traffic. And it stains from everything: tannins, rust, paint, and every automotive fluid known to man.
          </p>
          <p>
            A quality epoxy coating addresses all of these problems simultaneously. The cured epoxy film seals the concrete pores, eliminating dusting and dramatically reducing stain absorption. Its hard surface resists abrasion from tires and foot traffic. And cleanup becomes a matter of mopping rather than scrubbing — spilled oil sits on top of the coating rather than soaking into the slab.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">The Case for Epoxy</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
